SUMMARY:Old School Discussion: Consciousness-Raising Revisited
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\nBefore social media and algorit
 hmic outrage\, people gathered in small groups to seriously discuss how so
 ciety shapes personal life. During the Second Wave feminist movement (roug
 hly 1968–1975)\, consciousness-raising groups became a major organizing 
 tool. Feminists adapted aspects of the practice from earlier political and
  revolutionary discussion traditions\, including methods that emphasized c
 ollective analysis of everyday experience rather than isolated individual 
 struggle.\n\nThis 6-session series revisits the historic practice of consc
 iousness-raising through both historical and modern themes: gender roles\,
  work\, relationships\, power\, race\, care work\, violence\, media\, and 
 community.\n\nWomen and men are welcome. This is not therapy\, debate club
 \, or partisan organizing. The purpose is structured listening and collect
 ive reflection grounded in lived experience.\n\nEach session will include:
 \n\n* structured discussion grounded in lived experience\n* timed speaking
  rounds to encourage equal participation\n* the option to pass at any time
 \n* attentive listening without interruption or debate\n* guided reflectio
 n using the question: *Cui bono? — Who benefits?*\n* fact sheet and reso
 urce list related to the week’s theme\n\nParticipants will also help cho
 ose future discussion topics from historical consciousness-raising topic l
 ists.\n\nWe will return throughout the series to one guiding question:\n*C
 ui bono?* — Who benefits?\n\nFormat:\n\n* Facilitated by Susan\, LFS mem
 ber\n* 6 sessions total\n* 2 hours each\n* Small-group format (limited to 
 10 seats)\n* Respectful mixed-gender space\n* Consistent attendance encour
 aged\n\nClassic consciousness-raising guidelines emphasized listening with
 out interruption\, speaking from personal experience\, and recognizing tha
 t many “private” struggles are shaped by larger social systems. We’l
 l revisit that approach together in a calmer\, more thoughtful setting.\n\
 nNo homework. No expertise required.\nJust curiosity\, honesty\, and willi
 ngness to listen.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 314894523/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260521T171534Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260521T171534Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
